{
  "rationale": "Use a permissive plant with all sensing and motion events always available, then encode the safe exploration policy in a single deterministic specification automaton. The specification gives exactly one controllable action in each non-terminal decision/recovery state, blocks forward/random motion after any obstacle event, uses brief backward escape only for front obstacles, biases left/right obstacle recovery to the opposite turn direction, and returns quickly to exploration when path_clear is observed. Action states self-loop on path_clear so intended one-shot commands are not preempted, while obstacle events can still force safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model sensing and actuation separately in the plant so the supervisor is synthesized mainly from the specification.",
    "Use a small set of exploration, progress, and obstacle-recovery states with exactly one enabled controllable action per active state."
  ],
